The attached image is a Western blot (Figure 7D) illustrating the processing and secretion of IL-1β by dendritic cells treated with LPS and/or Nano-11. In the cell lysate, a 30 kD band, representing the inactive pro-IL-1β precursor, is evident when cells are primed with LPS. In the supernatant, LPS treatment alone results in a band around 20 kD, while Nano-11 treatment, particularly in LPS-primed cells, induces a strong 15 kD band, confirming the secretion of the active 17 kD form of IL-1β. This indicates Nano-11 effectively promotes the cleavage and release of active IL-1β, a crucial pro-inflammatory cytokine.